Dogs of War, Cops 'n' Robbers, Ninja Combat, Pit-Fighter, Time Pilot, Breakout
Star Trek (1971), 1943 (1987) and Raiden (1990) are historical gameplay inspirations. Neon Air draws on
air hockey. All new cabinet identities, settings and assets are original.

Their names identify the referenced games; no affiliation or endorsement is
implied. No original game assets or binaries are included.

The controller deadzone/neutral-arming logic and fixed-step clock refinements are
adapted from QSOLKCB/VANILLAJS (Apache-2.0). Performance changes follow the
optimization method of QSOLKCB/OPT (Apache-2.0); no OPT code is included.

js/vanilla2d.js is generated from QSOLKCB/VANILLAJS (Apache-2.0) modules motion2d,
range2d, audio2d and ternary-store2d by scripts/vanilla2d.cjs; the module bodies
are copied unchanged and the source commit is recorded in the file.


ARCADE 2 adds ten original cabinets inspired by the gameplay categories requested
by Trent Slade. The historical titles are listed in arcade2/README.md solely to
identify those inspirations. No commercial game assets or source are included.
Selected QSOLKCB/VANILLAJS v1.2.0 modules are preserved under
arcade2/vendor/vanillajs with their full LICENSE, NOTICE and pinned provenance.

ARCADE 3 adds nine original cabinets inspired by the gameplay of titles requested
by Trent Slade. Those titles are listed in arcade3/README.md solely to identify the
inspirations; no names, characters, levels, maps, art, music, sound or source from
those games are included, and no endorsement is implied. ARCADE 3 reuses the
ARCADE 2 runtime from arcade2/ and adds no third-party code.

ARCADE 2 v0.7.0:
- The integer CORDIC/BAM sine and cosine in arcade2/core.js (A.sinCosQ30) is a
  JavaScript port of sin_cos_q30 from QSOLKCB/GALAXY retro/src/lib.rs (Apache-2.0),
  checked against GALAXY's own reference vectors. The shooters' spiral-galaxy
  backdrop follows the look of GALAXY's renderer; no GALAXY rendering code is copied.
- The (2,3) torus-knot boss paths and the 2:3 "boss" sound cue are independent
  implementations of public mathematics, inspired by QSOLKCB/GLUBALL (MPL-2.0).
  No GLUBALL source is included.
- Ember Wing's Remix "Focus" is an integer adaptation of the QSOLKCB/VANILLAJS
  time-domains contract (Apache-2.0); no module code is copied.
